  "new_regression_evidence": [
    "The TUI action port freezes recorded evidence and submits a manually edited rubric through the local daemon; an unchanged retry creates no additional assessment.",
    "A stale corrected draft cannot replace a newer selected assessment; reopening a checkpoint loads its current rubric and revision.",
    "Mandatory criteria cannot become non-applicable, invalid scores are rejected, and a positive verification claim requires a recorded tool observation.",
    "Unknown values remain an interval with no complete reward. Evidence reading preserves a route back to the local review.",
    "An appended native session makes an earlier-prefix manual save explicitly stale and excluded from current learning, even when the historical submission receipt originally selected that revision.",
    "Judge-model configuration preserves the mode current at the transaction, including Off; mode changes use the real local operator interface.",
    "Local review identity remains usable after the coding transport disconnects, while operations-only targets do not expose the controls.",
    "A failed evaluation selection restores its source picker and preserves the unsent coding prompt.",
    "The chat architecture boundary still excludes direct database, metering, configuration and daemon access."
  ],
  "remaining_acceptance": [
